{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghWDzpL1Pprp5Z5uaNEg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The band positions give a rough Dq, but B cannot be determined from this data within the ligand-field model.\n\n**Dq:** For d⁹ in a regular octahedron there is one spin-allowed transition, ²Eg → ²T2g, at exactly 10Dq. Here the Jahn-Teller distortion of the axially elongated Cu(II) splits that band. Taking the band maximum (14 720 cm⁻¹) as the dominant component gives 10Dq ≈ 14 720 cm⁻¹, so Dq ≈ 1470 cm⁻¹. This is an approximation. Using the midpoint of the two observed features instead (≈13 480 cm⁻¹) would give ≈1350 cm⁻¹, so the uncertainty is roughly ±100 cm⁻¹.\n\n**B:** Not determinable. The d⁹ ground and excited term energies depend only on Dq (and the tetragonal distortion parameters) at the level of this model. The Racah parameter B does not enter the position of any d⁹ band, so a single broad band plus a shoulder cannot fix B. Obtaining B would need additional data, such as a d-d band from a different d^n ion in the same ligand set, or a spin-allowed band whose energy depends on B.\n\n**C:** Not determinable for the same reason.\n\n{\"Dq\": 1470, \"B\": null, \"C\": null, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Dq estimated as about 1470 cm-1 from the d9 band maximum (10Dq), with a Jahn-Teller uncertainty of roughly ±100 cm-1; B is not determinable because d9 band energies do not depend on B.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":218,"cache_read_input_tokens":627,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":218,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ccbe078e-412d-4327-a853-b345956ef7d8","uuid":"f9e73081-746e-